  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming Humanitarian Energy Access</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Transforming Humanitarian Energy Access (THEA) programme aims to deliver transformative action on clean energy access in humanitarian settings, working with the FCDO&#x2019;s Transforming Energy Access (TEA) platform to mainstream energy access in humanitarian settings and provide expert advice on the energy needs of refugees and internally displaced people (IDPs) for UK and international energy access partners. THEA is delivered by Mercy Corps, inpartnership with Refugee Led Organizations, Ashden and the Coordination Unit of the GlobalPlatform for Action (GPA CU) on Sustainable Energy in Displacement Settings (hosted at UNITAR).</narrative>
  </description>
